From: X2 bring-up <x2@local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a5xx: skip RBCCU bring-up before GPMU firmware init

The A530/A540 RBCCU and SP power domains are controlled by the GPMU.
On the first runtime resume, which runs before a5xx_hw_init() has had a
chance to load and start the GPMU firmware, polling the RBCCU GDSC
handshake times out and aborts the whole GPU bring-up. Keep the core
rail/clock setup, but postpone the RBCCU/SP domain sequence until the
GPMU firmware has been initialized.

Signed-off-by: X2 bring-up <x2@local>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a5xx_gpu.c
@@ -1353,5 +1353,6 @@ static int a5xx_pm_resume(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 {
 	struct adreno_gpu *adreno_gpu = to_adreno_gpu(gpu);
+	struct a5xx_gpu *a5xx_gpu = to_a5xx_gpu(adreno_gpu);
 	int ret;
 
 	/* Turn on the core power */
@@ -1370,6 +1371,16 @@ static int a5xx_pm_resume(struct msm_gpu *gpu)
 		return 0;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The GPMU owns the RBCCU/SP power domain handshake. a5xx_hw_init()
+	 * loads and starts the GPMU only after the first runtime resume, so
+	 * polling RBCCU before that just times out and aborts the whole GPU
+	 * bring-up. Keep the core rail/clock on and let hw_init start the
+	 * GPMU first.
+	 */
+	if (!a5xx_gpu->gpmu_ready)
+		return 0;
+
 	/* Turn the RBCCU domain first to limit the chances of voltage droop */
 	gpu_write(gpu, REG_A5XX_GPMU_RBCCU_POWER_CNTL, 0x778000);
 
